# Names ngspice's model has and Xyce's has not, at the value that is
# ngspice's default: nothing changes there (ngspice's BSIM3 ACM resistances
# and NQS switch, its BJT substrate current and emission coefficient).
noparam bsim3 rd=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 rd error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bsim3 rs=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 rs error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bsim3 rdc=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 rdc error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bsim3 rsc=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 rsc error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bsim3 hdif=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 hdif error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bsim3 ldif=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 ldif error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bsim3 nqsmod=0 warning : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bsim3 nqsmod error : Xyce's BSIM3 has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bjt iss=0 warning : Xyce's BJT has no such parameter; at 0, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bjt iss error : Xyce's BJT has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
noparam bjt ns=1 warning : Xyce's BJT has no such parameter; at 1, ngspice's default, it changes nothing
noparam bjt ns error : Xyce's BJT has no such parameter; the device is simulated without its effect
# VBIC's and PSP103's safe-operating-area parameters: Xyce's modules have
# none, so the check they ask for is not made, and no current changes.
noparam vbic vbe_max warning : Xyce's VBIC has no safe-operating-area check; vbe_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam vbic vbc_max warning : Xyce's VBIC has no safe-operating-area check; vbc_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam vbic vce_max warning : Xyce's VBIC has no safe-operating-area check; vce_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam vbic vsub_max warning : Xyce's VBIC has no safe-operating-area check; vsub_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 swsoa warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; swsoa changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 vgs_max warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; vgs_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 vgd_max warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; vgd_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 vgb_max warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; vgb_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 vds_max warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; vds_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 vsb_max warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; vsb_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
noparam psp103 vdb_max warning : Xyce's PSP103 has no safe-operating-area check; vdb_max changes no current there, and the check it asks for is not made
# A card's own value: whether Xyce gives it to a device that has none was
# not measured, and Xyce refuses a capacitor whose value is on its card.
noparam resistor r error : Xyce lists R among its resistor card's parameters, but not what a device without a value of its own takes from it; give the value on the instance

modelparams inductor
  same tc1
  # A card's L multiplies the line's own value (3 and 1 mH are 3 mH,
  # docs/verification.md 9.1): no other dialect's card has it.
  lscale = l
end
# docs/verification.md 9.1: "No model parameter IND found for model LMOD of
# type L, parameter ignored", and the line's own value is read.
noparam inductor ind warning : Xyce's inductor model has no IND, the inductance of a line that gives none; a line gives its own here, and one that gives none is refused whatever the card says
computes resistor narrow short : R = RSH (L - NARROW) / (W - NARROW), with no SHORT (a warning, and it is ignored)
no pattern : Xyce has no named bit patterns; a bit pattern is a PWL
# .FFT, as the Xyce source reads it (N_IO_FFTMgr.C, N_IO_FFTAnalysis.C):
# these keys only, the windows below (no gauss or kaiser), NP 1024, RECT
# and NORM unless given.
rule  fft       = ".fft" out { start=start from=start stop=stop to=stop np=np window=window alfa=alfa format=format freq=freq fmin=fmin fmax=fmax }
enum  fft window : rect=rect rect=rectangular bart=bart bart=bartlett bartletthann=bartletthann hamm=hamm hamm=hamming hann=hann hann=hanning black=black black=blackman harris=harris harris=blackmanharris nuttall=nuttall halfcyclesine=halfcyclesine halfcyclesine3=halfcyclesine3 halfcyclesine6=halfcyclesine6 cosine2=cosine2 cosine4=cosine4
enum  fft format : norm=norm unorm=unorm
no optimize : Xyce has no optimizer statement (Dakota drives Xyce from outside)
# Families ngspice has that Xyce has no model of (#48).
no model mos9 : Xyce's M levels (DeviceModelPKG registerDevice) are 1, 2, 3, 6, 9 and 49 (BSIM3), 10 and 57 (BSIM3SOI 3.2), 14 and 54, 18, 70, 77, 103, 107 to 111 and others; none is SPICE3's MOS9 (Xyce's level 9 is BSIM3)
no model bsim1 : Xyce's M levels (DeviceModelPKG registerDevice) are 1, 2, 3, 6, 9 and 49 (BSIM3), 10 and 57 (BSIM3SOI 3.2), 14 and 54, 18, 70, 77, 103, 107 to 111 and others; none is BSIM1
no model bsim2 : Xyce's M levels (DeviceModelPKG registerDevice) are 1, 2, 3, 6, 9 and 49 (BSIM3), 10 and 57 (BSIM3SOI 3.2), 14 and 54, 18, 70, 77, 103, 107 to 111 and others; none is BSIM2
no model b3soifd : Xyce's BSIM3SOI (levels 10 and 57) is version 3.2 and read here as bsimsoi; ngspice's fully depleted B3SOIFD 2.1 is another model
no model b3soidd : Xyce's BSIM3SOI (levels 10 and 57) is version 3.2 and read here as bsimsoi; ngspice's dynamically depleted B3SOIDD 2.1 is another model
no model b3soipd : Xyce's BSIM3SOI (levels 10 and 57) is version 3.2 and read here as bsimsoi; that it takes ngspice's B3SOIPD 2.2.3 cards unchanged is not measured
no model mesa : Xyce's MESFET (Z) has one level (N_DEV_MESFET.C registers z level 1), not MESA
no model urc : Xyce's U is a digital device; `U1 in out 0 umod L=100u N=10` stops Xyce 7.10 ("Unrecognized parameter OUT for device UIN!1", docs/verification.md 4.29)
no script : Xyce has no control script; its analyses and outputs are netlist lines
no csparam : only a control script reads a .csparam vector, and xyce has none
no native : the statement is another dialect's own, which no kind holds; only that dialect writes it
no embed : VACASK embeds a file (a post-processing script) in the netlist; this dialect has no such statement, so save the file next to the netlist
